CAVECODE SPEC — BASTION RUNNER (ARC-CR-001)
Category: cavern-run
Engine: Side-view runner with five levels
Version: 1.3

🪨 BLOCK 1 — IDENTITY
Title: Cavern Run — Bastion Runner
Game ID: ARC-CR-001
Goal: Jump grounded hazards, collect coins and reach each distance target.

🎮 BLOCK 2 — CORE LOOP / BEHAVIOR
- Wait for Start Level before moving or spawning. Restart returns to Ready.
- Exactly one requestAnimationFrame loop per run; cancel it before restarting.
- Measure jump position in pixels and velocity in pixels/second, upward positive.
- Advance position with v*dt + 0.5*g*dt*dt, then velocity with g*dt.
- Land at zero height. Reject a second jump immediately after takeoff.
- Cap frame delta at 50ms; reset the time anchor on visibility changes.
- Move hazards left with level speed. Ground hazards sit on the ground;
  coins float 36-64px above it.
- Each hazard can cost one life. Three lives per level; zero ends the run.
- Coins increase chain by 0.2 up to 3.5 and add 5*chain to distance.
  A hit resets chain to 1.
- Reach target AND at least 20 seconds of play to clear the level and unlock Next Level. Never skip uncleared levels.
- Result modal stays available until the player chooses restart/replay/next.
- Completing level five permits looping back to level one.
- Best distance is session-only and measures an individual level attempt.

🕹️ BLOCK 3 — INPUT
Space / W / ArrowUp, Jump button, or press playfield: jump if grounded.
Touch, pen and primary mouse input fire on pointerdown (contact), not release.
Ignore the following pointer click so release never queues a second jump.
Ignore secondary touches/right-clicks and repeated held keyboard keydowns.
Keyboard/assistive click activation remains supported.
Start Level: begin the ready level.
Restart Run: reset current level to Ready with three lives and zero distance.
Next Level: available only after clearing the current level.

🎚️ BLOCK 4 — TUNING KNOBS (HUMAN EDIT ZONE)
GRAVITY: -1400           # pixels / second squared
JUMP_VELOCITY: 520       # pixels / second
MAX_FRAME_MS: 50
livesPerLevel: 3
Level name          | target | speed (units/s) | spawn(ms) | approach(s) | coinChance
Warm-Up Cavern      | 400    | 20              | 1800      | 2.2         | 0.25
Low Ceiling Run     | 650    | 24              | 1650      | 2.0         | 0.30
Shardfall Tunnel    | 900    | 28              | 1500      | 1.9         | 0.35
Breaker Gallery    | 1200   | 32              | 1400      | 1.8         | 0.40
Deep Bastion        | 1600   | 36              | 1300      | 1.7         | 0.45
Hazard speed = max(80, playfieldWidth*0.86-32) / approachSeconds pixels/s.
Phone layout hides the verbose overview and keeps HUD, track and large Jump visible.
Executable values live in index.html. Keep this companion map synchronized.

🌐 BLOCK 5 — PUBLIC TEXT
Title: Bastion Runner
Buttons: Start Level / Jump / Restart Run / Next Level
Results: Level Clear / Deep Bastion Clear / Run Lost
HUD: Level / Distance / Target / Lives / Best Run / Jumps

📝 BLOCK 10 — HUMAN NOTES
The prior companion described an earlier one-hit endless runner. This version
maps the existing five-level implementation and its gameplay repairs.
Regression checks: node tests/gameplay-regressions.cjs from repository root.
The tests cover logic and simulated event bubbling, not browser rendering.
